msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:51
msgid "Shortens the addresses visitors see, such as \"Edinburgh\" instead of \"Edinburgh, Scotland, United Kingdom\". Stored addresses are left alone unless the Saved Value setting is ticked, so you can switch back at any time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:56
msgid "Address Format"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:57
msgid "How much of each saved address to show. Addresses are split on commas, counted from the left. Themes that draw their own address line (ExpertHive, JobHive, MeetingHive) keep it, so this has no effect there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:69
msgid "A set number of parts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:74
msgid "Number of Parts (used with \"A set number of parts\")"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:75
msgid "How many comma separated parts to show, counted from the left."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:84
msgid "Repeated Parts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:85
msgid "Some providers repeat a part, such as \"Edinburgh, Edinburgh, Scotland\". Tick this to show each repeated part once, wherever addresses appear."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:86
msgid "Remove repeated address parts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:92
msgid "Listing Address Format"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:93
msgid "Overrides the Address Format above for listing locations only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:101
msgid "Listing Address Length (characters)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:102
msgid "Trims the displayed listing address to this many characters, ending with an ellipsis. Leave it empty for no limit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:111
msgid "Vendor Address Format"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:112
msgid "Overrides the Address Format above for vendor locations only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:120
msgid "Vendor Address Length (characters)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:121
msgid "Trims the displayed vendor address to this many characters, ending with an ellipsis. Leave it empty for no limit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:130
msgid "Saved Value"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:131
msgid "By default the full address is saved and only shortened for display. Tick this to save the shortened address as people pick a suggestion. Existing entries are not changed. Uses the main Address Format above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:132
msgid "Save the shortened address instead"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:140
msgid "Location Suggestions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:141
msgid "Controls the list of places offered while somebody types in a location field. Restricting it is the tidiest way to keep saved locations consistent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:146
msgid "Suggestion Types"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:147
msgid "The kinds of place people may choose. Leave it empty to allow everything. Applies to the main location field only, never to the Location attributes you create. Geocoders vary in how strictly they honour this."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:154
msgid "Country"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:155
msgid "Region"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:156
msgid "Subregion"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:157
msgid "City"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:158
msgid "District"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:159
msgid "Postcode"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:160
msgid "Street address"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:165
msgid "Places of Interest"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:166
msgid "Hides named venues such as \"Edinburgh Castle\" from the suggestion list, so people pick addresses and place names instead. Applies to the main location field only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:167
msgid "Hide places of interest from suggestions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:173
msgid "Shorten Suggestions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:174
msgid "Shows each suggestion already shortened by the Address Format. With Google Maps or Mapbox selected the built-in location field draws its own list, which cannot be shortened."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:175
msgid "Apply the Address Format to suggestions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:181
msgid "Minimum Length (characters)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:182
msgid "How many characters must be typed before suggestions are requested. Raising it cuts requests to your geocoder, which matters on the free plans. Google Maps and Mapbox ignore this for the built-in location field."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:194
msgid "Map Appearance"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:195
msgid "Applies to maps drawn by the map providers this plugin adds. Google Maps and Mapbox draw their own maps and are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:200
msgid "Map Style"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:201
msgid "The look of the map itself. The choices depend on which map provider is selected, so save the provider first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:209
msgid "Marker Colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:210
msgid "The colour of the pins on the map, as a six digit hex code such as #ff5a5f. Leave it empty for the default blue (#3a77ff)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:219
#: includes/configs/settings.php:225
msgid "Service Areas"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:220
msgid "For vendors who travel to their customers. A vendor sets how far they travel, and their listings then appear in location searches for anyone inside that distance, even when that is further than the searcher's own radius."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:226
msgid "Adds a Service Radius field to the vendor profile. Leaving it empty means customers come to the vendor, so nothing changes for vendors who do not travel."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:227
msgid "Let vendors set how far they travel"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:234
msgid "Longest Service Radius (miles)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:235
msgid "Longest Service Radius (km)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:236
msgid "The most a vendor can enter. Uses the same unit as the search radius above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:246
msgid "Travelling Listings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:247
msgid "Which of a travelling vendor's listings use their service area. Choose an attribute option if only some listings are carried out at the customer's address, for example a \"Where\" attribute with an \"At your address\" option."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:249
msgid "Every listing of a vendor who travels"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:257
msgid "Customer Address for Bookings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:258
msgid "The booking field where customers enter the address the vendor travels to. Choosing one adds Travel Fee fields to the vendor profile, charges the fee at checkout and refuses addresses outside the vendor's service area. Only Location fields from this plugin appear here, because they store the map position the distance is measured from."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:260
msgid "None (no travel fees)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:269
msgid "Distance Included in the Travel Fee (miles)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:270
msgid "Distance Included in the Travel Fee (km)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:271
msgid "The per-mile or per-km part of a vendor's travel fee starts after this distance, measured in a straight line from the listing. Leave it at 0 to charge from the first mile or km."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:283
msgid "Removing the Plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:284
msgid "What happens to these settings if you ever delete Geolocation Plus. They are kept by default, so reinstalling restores everything. Ignore the generic warning WordPress shows when deleting a plugin; the setting below is what counts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:289
msgid "Deleting the Plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:290
msgid "Tick this only if you want everything removed for good, which cannot be undone. It removes every setting on this page and the API keys in the Integrations section."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:291
msgid "Delete all data when this plugin is deleted"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:305
msgid "Only used when MapTiler is selected as the map provider. Create a free account at maptiler.com and copy the key from the Keys page. Restrict the key to your own domain first: it is readable by anyone who views the page. Widest choice of map styles. In the United Kingdom a listing in a large city can be filed under a named district of it, such as Old Town in Edinburgh."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:320
msgid "Only used when Geoapify is selected as the map provider. Create a free account at geoapify.com, add a project and copy the API key. Restrict the key to your own domain first: it is readable by anyone who views the page. Names places consistently, though it abbreviates some labels, such as England to \"ENG\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:335
msgid "Only used when LocationIQ is selected as the map provider. Create a free account at locationiq.com and copy the access token from the Dashboard. Restrict the key to your own domain first: it is readable by anyone who views the page. The most detailed addresses of the three; the free plan allows about one search a second. It sometimes names a city by its council area, such as \"Aberdeen City\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:350
msgid "Only used when HERE is selected as the map provider. Sign up for the free Base plan at platform.here.com, open Access Manager, register an app, then create an API key on its Credentials tab. Add your domain under the key's trusted domains first: it is readable by anyone who views the page. One key covers the map, suggestions and region lookups, and the free plan includes a monthly allowance of each."
msgstr ""

